# ── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pnpm creates node_modules in the root (the real store links) AND in each
# package (symlinks such as apps/server/node_modules/@jejune/shared).
# This one pattern covers all of them.
node_modules/

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `vite build` writes apps/web/dist. Any future server bundle would land in a
# dist/ folder too. These are always regenerated, so never commit them.
dist/
# TypeScript's incremental-build cache (only appears if "incremental" or
# project references get turned on later).
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Local data (SQLite) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app's database holds YOUR projects, conversations, and tasks. It's user
# data, not source code. In WAL mode SQLite also writes "-wal" and "-shm"
# sidecar files next to the main file. The trailing "*" catches those too
# (app.db, app.db-wal, app.db-shm).
*.db*
*.sqlite*
# NOTE: Drizzle *migrations* (generated .sql files) are source code and SHOULD
# be committed. Those patterns don't match .sql, so they're safe.

# ── Secrets / local config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env files will hold the optional OpenAI API key (PLAN §3.2). Never commit them.
# The negation lets you commit an example file listing the variable NAMES
# (with no real values) as documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pino logs written to disk, plus the debug logs pnpm writes when an install fails.
*.log
logs/

# ── Test output (Playwright, Vitest coverage) ───────────────────────────────
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/
coverage/

# ── OS / editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS writes .DS_Store in every folder you open in Finder.
.DS_Store
# Editor settings are personal. If you later want to share specific files
# (e.g. .vscode/extensions.json), re-include them with "!".
.vscode/
.idea/
